                <pb facs="0333" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/1197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-05T11:00:00+01:00">October 5, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 5—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Referring to my telegram No. 55, August 26, 11 a.m. and Department’s 46,
                    August 27, 2 p.m.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d320-f1"/> Having received no reply to
                    my personal note of August 29, I telephoned Señor Vidal today. He stated it was
                    wholly impossible to consider the release of American prisoners but he would be
                    glad to receive any concrete proposal for their exchange. My impression is that
                    Burgos authorities do not want to act in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
